<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, October to November is the driest pair here at 5.17 inches normal, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids it came in under 90% of normal in 42 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 that pair ran 44% of normal on the middle of the grids, and September to October ran 41%. This year so far, March to April 2026 came in at 26% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 15191 at 46%.</p>"}
